  "question": {
    "text": "If the system of equations\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& 2 x+7 y+\\lambda z=3 \\\\\n& 3 x+2 y+5 z=4 \\\\\n& x+\\mu y+32 z=-1\n\\end{aligned}$\nhas infinitely many solutions, then $(\\lambda-\\mu)$ is equal to________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "38",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{D}=\\mathrm{D}_1=\\mathrm{D}_2=\\mathrm{D}_3=0 \\\\ & \\mathrm{D}_3=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}2 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & \\mu & -1\\end{array}\\right|=0 \\Rightarrow \\mu=-39 \\\\ & \\mathrm{D}=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}2 & 7 & \\lambda \\\\ 3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -39 & 32\\end{array}\\right|=0 \\Rightarrow \\lambda=-1 \\\\ & \\lambda-\\mu=38\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
